At 844x390: topbar 12, hud 56 (height ~40), play top bound 96. Touch controls bottom 21-131, xp bottom 142. Player bottom H-128=262, so the touch controls area is 259-390; player max y 262, just above controls. Good. XP at 142 → y=248, just above controls and below player. Hmm xp overlaps player area slightly but thin.

Welcome: title font clamp(34, 34.3, 54)=34.3px — very small; 2 lines = 65px. Intro 2 lines 35px; kicker 20; button 40; best 15 → total ~200. Centered in 390. Good.

But wait, the welcome-screen at compact uses `padding-left:9%` and `.welcome-copy{width:330px}`. 844 width, content at x=76. The ship preview at x=.69*844=582, y=195 — to the right of text. Nice. Annotations hidden. Good.

Touch controls at 844 width: left 14, right 14; dpad at left, fire at right. Good. They're big but fine.

One issue: mobile media `.welcome-screen{padding-left:8%;align-items:center}` comes before; compact overrides 9%.

Also the compact hud at top 56; the brand at 12. Good.

Let's add this block.

